  "title": "Why does a compass point north? 🧭",
  "hook": "Why does a compass needle always point north?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_hook",
      "narration": "Why does a compass needle always point north?",
      "on_screen_text": "Why does it point north?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "north?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_magnet",
      "narration": "Because the needle is a magnet, and every magnet makes an invisible magnetic field around it.",
      "on_screen_text": "An invisible field",
      "highlight_words": [
        "invisible"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_domains",
      "narration": "Inside a magnet, millions of tiny magnetic regions all point the same way.",
      "on_screen_text": "All lined up",
      "highlight_words": [
        "lined"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_poles",
      "narration": "And their poles work like this: like poles repel and opposites attract.",
      "on_screen_text": "Opposites attract",
      "highlight_words": [
        "attract"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_core",
      "narration": "The whole Earth is a giant magnet, thanks to liquid iron swirling in its core.",
      "on_screen_text": "Earth is a magnet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "magnet"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_north",
      "narration": "The needle points to magnetic north, which funnily enough is a magnetic south pole: that's why it pulls the needle's north end.",
      "on_screen_text": "North is a south pole",
      "highlight_words": [
        "south"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_moving",
      "narration": "And that pole isn't fixed: it moves tens of kilometers every year.",
      "on_screen_text": "The pole moves",
      "highlight_words": [
        "moves"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_animals",
      "narration": "Sea turtles and migrating birds use this field like a natural GPS.",
      "on_screen_text": "A natural GPS",
      "highlight_words": [
        "GPS"
      ],
      "sfx": "bubbles",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_flip",
      "narration": "And every so often the field flips completely: the last time was about seven hundred eighty thousand years ago.",
      "on_screen_text": "The field flips!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "flips!"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
