  "description": "A compass needle is a magnet; inside a magnet the magnetic domains are aligned, and opposite poles attract. Earth is a giant magnet because of moving liquid iron in its core, and the magnetic north the needle points to is actually a magnetic south pole. That pole drifts tens of km a year, many animals navigate by the field, and the field flips every so often: the last time about 780,000 years ago. Original 3D animation.",
